# Sigma.js V3 Implementation Reference

## V3 Breaking Changes
- **Constructor**: `new Sigma(graph, container, settings)` - graph parameter now required first
- **Package Structure**: Official extensions under `@sigma/` namespace, monorepo with Preconstruct
- **Current**: v3.0.1 (August 2024), testing phase but production-ready

## V3 Architecture Improvements
- **Instanced Rendering**: Attributes sent once per element, not per vertex (major memory reduction)
- **Picking System**: Built-in collision detection eliminates manual quadtree management
- **Optimized Indexing**: Only affected indexes modified on updates vs full re-indexing
- **TypeScript Generics**: Full type safety for graph data structures

## Advanced Node/Edge Attributes

**Node Attributes**:

{
  x: number, y: number, size: number, color: string, // required
  label?: string, type?: string, // connects to nodeProgramClasses key
  hidden?: boolean, forceLabel?: boolean, zIndex?: number
}


**Edge Attributes**:

{
  size?: number, color?: string, type?: string, // connects to edgeProgramClasses key  
  hidden?: boolean, forceLabel?: boolean, zIndex?: number,
  curvature?: number // for @sigma/edge-curve
}


**Critical**: `type` values must match keys in `nodeProgramClasses`/`edgeProgramClasses` or default renderers used.

## Layer Architecture & Z-Index
**Rendering Order**: `sigma-edges` → `sigma-nodes` → `sigma-labels` → `sigma-hovers` → `sigma-hoverNodes` → `sigma-mouse`

**Z-Index Control**:

// Enable z-index sorting (performance cost)
const sigma = new Sigma(graph, container, { zIndex: true });

// Higher zIndex values render on top
graph.updateNodeAttribute("node1", "zIndex", 10);

**Limitation**: Edges never render above nodes regardless of zIndex.

## Performance Optimizations

**Skip Re-indexing**:

sigma.refresh({ skipIndexation: true }); // when topology unchanged


**Batch Operations**:

graph.emit('startBatch');
// multiple graph modifications
graph.emit('endBatch');


**Edge Performance**: `edgequad.prototype.index` bottleneck for >17k edges. Use `drawEdges: false` during interactions.

**Memory Management**:

// Critical cleanup sequence
sigma.off('clickNode'); // remove listeners first
sigma.kill(); // disposes WebGL contexts
container.innerHTML = ''; // clear DOM


## Advanced Program Classes

**Multiple Renderers**:

const sigma = new Sigma(graph, container, {
  nodeProgramClasses: {
    circle: NodeCircleProgram, // default
    image: NodeImageProgram,
    square: NodeSquareProgram,
    gradient: CustomGradientProgram
  },
  edgeProgramClasses: {
    line: EdgeLineProgram, // default
    curved: EdgeCurveProgram,
    arrow: EdgeArrowProgram
  }
});


**Custom Programs**: Require vertex shader (.vert.glsl), fragment shader (.frag.glsl), and program class extending NodeProgram/EdgeProgram.

## Reducers (Dynamic Styling)

**Advanced Reducer Patterns**:

// Context-aware reducer with performance optimization
const nodeReducer = (node, data) => {
  if (selectedNodes.has(node.id)) {
    return { ...data, size: data.size * 1.5, zIndex: 999 };
  }
  if (hoveredNeighbors.has(node.id)) {
    return { ...data, color: data.highlightColor || data.color };
  }
  return selectedNodes.size > 0 ? { ...data, color: "#ddd" } : data;
};

sigma.setSetting("nodeReducer", nodeReducer);


## Official @sigma Extensions

**Node Renderers**:
- `@sigma/node-image` (v3.0.0): Texture atlas, multiple textures, maxTextureSize: 4096
- `@sigma/node-border` (v3.0.0): Concentric discs with borderColor attribute
- `@sigma/node-square` (v3.0.0): Square nodes

**Edge Renderers**:
- `@sigma/edge-curve` (v3.1.0): Quadratic Bézier with curvature parameter

**Layer Extensions**:
- `@sigma/layer-webgl`: Custom WebGL layer helpers
- `@sigma/layer-leaflet`/`@sigma/layer-maplibre`: Map integration

## Custom Layer Management

**Creating Custom Layers**:

const customCanvas = sigma.createCanvas({ 
  beforeLayer: "sigma-hovers" // insert before specific layer
});
const ctx = sigma.createCanvasContext(customCanvas);
// Custom drawing operations


**Layer Manipulation**:

// Insert custom HTML layer
const customLayer = document.createElement('div');
customLayer.style.position = 'absolute';
customLayer.style.inset = '0';
sigmaContainer.insertBefore(customLayer, sigmaContainer.querySelector('.sigma-hovers'));


## WebGL Program Development

**NodeProgram Requirements**:
- Vertex shader: transforms coordinates to screen position
- Fragment shader: determines pixel colors
- Program class: manages data bindings and lifecycle
- Picking support: unique colors for collision detection

**Performance Considerations**:
- NodePointProgram: Efficient but limited to 100px radius (gl.POINTS limitation)
- NodeCircleProgram: No size limits, uses triangles, more memory

## Event Handling & Interaction

**Typed Events**:

sigma.on("clickNode", ({ node, event }) => {
  // event: { x, y, originalEvent }
});

// Prevent default camera behavior
sigma.on("downStage", (e) => e.preventSigmaDefault());


**forceLabel Behavior**: Setting `forceLabel: true` on nodes automatically enables connected edge labels (side effect).

## Advanced Settings

**Size & Position Control**:

{
  itemSizesReference: "positions", // same coordinate system for sizes/positions
  autoRescale: false, // disable auto-rescaling for pixel-based positioning
  zoomToSizeRatioFunction: (ratio) => ratio // linear scaling vs default sqrt(ratio)
}


**Label Rendering**:

{
  defaultDrawNodeLabel: customLabelFunction,
  defaultDrawNodeHover: customHoverFunction,
  renderEdgeLabels: true // performance impact with many edges
}




